/Title (The foundation of this project was based on the problem specification from the Google Hash Code 2018 Online Qualification Round, the "Self-Driving Rides" optimization challenge.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 290 0 R
/Next 783 0 R
>>
endobj
642 0 obj
<<
/Title (Furthermore, the theoretical framework guiding our project came from our classes and from Stuart Russell and Peter Norvig's foundational textbook, "Artificial Intelligence: A Modern Approach.")
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 290 0 R
/Prev 784 0 R
>>
endobj
643 0 obj
<<
/Title (-Our experimental results also illustrate the inherent trade-offs between algorithms, showing that while the Greedy approach provides the best time-to-quality ratio for immediate execution, Simulated Annealing is strictly superior for offline, pre-planned routing maximization.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 23 0 R
/Prev 291 0 R
/Next 644 0 R
>>
endobj
644 0 obj
<<
/Title (-Additionally, our evaluation function successfully mirrored real-world logistics through a bin packing behavior, optimizing fleet usage by leaving unneeded vehicles idle rather than dispatching them on costly, empty trips.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 23 0 R
/Prev 643 0 R
/Next 292 0 R
>>
endobj
